    (b) and (c), the license granted under this Section is irrevocable
    and applies to the full scope of each Contributor's Rights in the
    Work, except that Trademark Rights are governed exclusively by
    subsection (c).

    (b) Design. To the extent a Contributor's Rights include Design
    embodied in the Work and disclosed by the Source form, the license
    granted under this Section with respect to such Design:

        (i)    is irrevocable;

        (ii)   applies only to those Design claims licensable by such
               Contributor that are necessarily infringed by their
               Contribution(s) alone or by combination of their
               Contribution(s) with the Work to which such
               Contribution(s) was submitted;

        (iii)  extends to modification of the Design and the creation
               of original designs based on the Work, with any such
               modification or original design itself constituting a
               Derivative Work for purposes of this License and
               subject, as such, to the redistribution conditions of
               Section 4;

        (iv)   with respect to an Object form, grants rights in any
               Design embodied therein only to the extent that the
               Right Holder has disclosed such Design through the
               Source form;

        (v)    with respect to a Physical Object Form, grants rights in
               any Design embodied therein only to the extent that the
               Right Holder has disclosed such Design through the
               Source form;

        (vi)   where You receive only the Source form, grants rights in
               any Design embodied therein only to the extent that such
               Design is disclosed in that Source form; and

        (vii)  nothing in this subsection (b) grants You any right to
               require, compel, or otherwise extend disclosure of the
               Source form of the Work or any Design embodied in
               Physical Object Form.

        (viii) if You institute litigation against any entity
               (including a cross-claim or counterclaim in a lawsuit)
               alleging that the Work or a Contribution incorporated
               within the Work infringes a Design right, then any
               Design license granted to You under this subsection (b)
               for that Work shall terminate as of the date such
               litigation is filed.

    (c) Trademarks. Notwithstanding subsection (a), the license granted
    under this Section with respect to Trademark Rights is limited to
    the uses expressly permitted under Section 8. No broader license to
    use, reproduce, display, or sublicense any trade name, trademark,
    service mark, or product name of the Right Holder is granted under
